The resource handler skips to a requested range's first byte and tells CEF the body's
length. CEF asks the handler to skip when the request carries a Range header; without
this method the default refuses, and every range past byte 0 fails with
ERR_REQUEST_RANGE_NOT_SATISFIABLE (ADR 0028). Applied by scripts/prepare-runtime-cef.sh.
Reported upstream as tauri-apps/tauri#16479; drop the patch when a released runtime has it.

